  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance and Capacity Building for the Government of Ukraine &#x2013; Developing and Implementing Interim Reparative Measures and Reparations for Survivors of Conflict-Related Sexual Violence</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The full-scale invasion of Ukraine, which started in February 2022, and the preceding hostilities in the Donbas and Crimea regions since 2014, have been characterised by the commission of numerous human rights violations. The project aims to contribute to the development and implementation of inclusive, timely, and effective policies and legal frameworks that ensure the provision of reparations to conflict-affected populations in Ukraine by providing the Government of Ukraine (GoU) with context-specific tools, knowledge, and a strategy.</narrative>
  </description>
